<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Exarchate of Africa</h1><p class="st-meta">591 CE – 698 CE (approx.) · capital Carthage</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Byzantine government of North Africa, a frontier exarchate at Carthage that launched Heraclius to the imperial throne.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 591 the emperor Maurice replaced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/praetorian-prefecture-of-africa">Praetorian Prefecture of Africa</a> with an exarchate, uniting civil and military authority in one governor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> to face <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> pressure. The first known exarch was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gennadius-exarch-of-africa">Gennadius</a>, who had defeated the Berber king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garmul">Garmul</a> in 578.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The exarchate covered the coast from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tripolitania">Tripolitania</a> to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/septem">Septem</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a>, and drew wealth from grain and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil">olive oil</a>. In 608 the exarch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius-the-elder">Heraclius the Elder</a> revolted against the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phocas">Phocas</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraclius">Heraclius</a> sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 610. In 646 the exarch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-the-patrician">Gregory the Patrician</a> declared himself emperor, but was killed by an Arab army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufetula">Sufetula</a> in 647.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Arab raids grew into conquest. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hassan-ibn-al-numan">Hassan ibn al-Numan</a> in 695, was briefly retaken in 697 and fell for good in 698 to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> built up nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, an ancient town, as their base, and only <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/septem">Septem</a> held out until around 711.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/exarchate-of-africa.jpg" alt="Exarchate of Africa" width="320" height="170"><figcaption>Image: Shuaaa2 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Exarchate_of_Africa_-_600_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>591 CE – 698 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Carthage</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gennadius, Heraclius the Elder, Gregory the Patrician</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chalcedonian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a>, <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Exarchate of Carthage</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=644&amp;focus=exarchate-of-africa" aria-label="Exarchate of Africa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4939 850 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Exarchate of Africa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5259 1106L5259 1106M5259 1106L5709 970M5259 1106L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0M5709 970h0M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5259 1106h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Carthage. <a href="/atlas?year=644&amp;focus=exarchate-of-africa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
